From bf20096d415b47664fc4a7685d4f0dd6ceaccfc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guilhem Bichot <guilhem.bichot@contributor>


Date: Wed, 12 Nov 2025 16:37:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] USERSTORY LEFT JOIN elimination

Join elimination is a feature found in prominent DBMSs.

Its principle is that, sometimes, a table can be removed from a join
without changing the query's result.

There exists inner join elimination and outer (=left) join elimination.

We implement only left-join elimination (LJE). Because inner-join
elimination is more complex and has not been requested by our
customers.

We do elimination in three cases: GROUP BY / DISTINCT, joining on
UNIQUE key, and when the join is inside a semi-join or anti-join or
related subqueries.
For joining on UNIQUE key, we also sometimes use, in certain types of
materialized derived tables, combinations of columns which form a sort of unique
key (this happens when the definition of the derived table contains GROUP BY
or DISTINCT).

Suggested first reading: the big Doxygen comment at the beginning of
sql/sql_join_elimination.cc . Next, to see the effects, you can look
at test join_elimination.test .

Design is at <internal-url-removed> .

The feature also has effects on lots of queries created by random
query generators and found in subquery.inc and subquery_sj.inc . To
preserve the intention of these tests and others, the feature is
disabled in them when needed, by using a new flag in optimizer_switch : left_join_elimination=on|off (on by default).

If you want a blog which covers the topic:
https://blog.jooq.org/join-elimination-an-essential-optimiser-feature-for-advanced-sql-usage/

If you want to read about what other products do:
https://docs.w3cub.com/mariadb/table-elimination-in-mariadb/index
https://www.alibabacloud.com/help/en/polardb/polardb-for-mysql/user-guide/left-join-elimination
https://www.alibabacloud.com/blog/about-database-kernel-%7C-polardb-optimizer-query-transformation---join-elimination_600497
https://open.oceanbase.com/blog/10900337
